{"abstract":[{"text":"Extend the formatting language with your own directives, or remove standard ones.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CustomDirectives"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"CLFormat"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Adding custom directives"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The directives that are available for a control string are defined by a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"configuration maps directive characters to parsers. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/standard","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" implements all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard directives. Copy it and modify the copy to define your own formatting language:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var config = CLFormatConfig.standard","config.remove(\"W\", \"w\")                       // remove directive ~W","config.parse(\"Z\", appending: ReverseSpecifier())","","try clformat(\"~Z\", config: config, args: \"abc\")    // \"cba\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Implementing-a-directive","level":3,"text":"Implementing a directive","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A directive is implemented by a type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/DirectiveSpecifier","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". It identifies the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directive character and interprets the parameters, modifiers, and arguments of a directive when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it is applied. Directive specifiers must be ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" since parsed controls can be shared","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between threads.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ReverseSpecifier: DirectiveSpecifier {","  var identifier: Character { return \"Z\" }","  var description: String { return \"Z\" }","  func apply(context: Context,","             parameters: Parameters,","             modifiers: Modifiers,","             arguments: Arguments) throws -> Instruction {","    return .append(String(try arguments.nextAsString().reversed()))","  }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Specifiers return an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/Instruction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"append","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" adds text to the output, ","type":"text"},{"code":"continue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ends the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"current iteration, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"break","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves the enclosing iteration.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Custom-directive-parsers","level":3,"text":"Custom directive parsers","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Most directives do not need special parsing because the control string parser handles","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameters and modifiers generically. Composite directives, such as iterations, parse the part","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the control string they enclose. For these, register a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/DirectiveParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" which receives the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLControlParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and returns a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/ParseResult","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["config.parse(\"y\", \"Y\") { parser, parameters, modifiers in","  return .append(parameters, modifiers, StandardDirectiveSpecifier.decimal)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Custom-arguments-and-global-defaults","level":3,"text":"Custom arguments and global defaults","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/setArgumentFactory(makeArguments:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" replaces the factory for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/Arguments","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" objects that provide the arguments to directives. A subclass of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/Arguments","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can, for instance, change which values count as ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or as boolean values.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/environment","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" stores additional values for custom directives, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/nilRepresentation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" determines how ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is printed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/default","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is used by ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/clformat(_:config:locale:tabsize:linewidth:displayWidth:args:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/clprintf(_:config:locale:tabsize:linewidth:displayWidth:args:terminator:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" if no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"configuration is passed explicitly. Reading and writing it is thread-safe, but modifying single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties is not atomic, so configure it once at startup.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat":{"abstract":[{"text":"Format text with the expressive control strings of Common Lisp’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"format","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"CLFormat","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/clformat"},"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/Arguments":{"abstract":[{"text":"Class ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arguments","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is used to encapsulate arguments and environment variables.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An instance of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arguments","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is passed to the format function when interpreting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the control string. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Argument","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects cannot be reused. They can only be used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once to format a string.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Arguments"}],"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/Arguments","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Arguments"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Arguments","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/clformat/arguments"},"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLControlParser":{"abstract":[{"text":"Implementation of a control string parser. The parser implements a generic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directive parser which then triggers directive-specific parsers that handle","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"composite directives (such as conversion, iteration, justification, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conditional directives).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CLControlParser"}],"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLControlParser","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CLControlParser"}],"role":"symbol","title":"CLControlParser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/clformat/clcontrolparser"},"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig":{"abstract":[{"text":"A format configuration value contains an argument factory, a default representation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as well as a mapping from directive identifiers (characters) to directive","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parsers which parse the directive. Most directives are atomic (i.e. they are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"composite) and parsing for those is trivial: they just package up the generically","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parsed parameters and modifiers in a new directive specifier value. Composite","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directives have more complex parsing logic.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CLFormatConfig"}],"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CLFormatConfig"}],"role":"symbol","title":"CLFormatConfig","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/clformat/clformatconfig"},"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/default":{"abstract":[{"text":"The default format configuration for the functions ","type":"text"},{"code":"clformat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"clprintf","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"configuation is mutable so that the behavior can be changed globally. Please note","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that the ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" initializers do not rely on this mutable config as a default.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"`default`"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8CLFormat0A6ConfigV","text":"CLFormatConfig"}],"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/default","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"default","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/clformat/clformatconfig/default"},"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/environment":{"abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"environment"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"Any"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/environment","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"environment","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/clformat/clformatconfig/environment"},"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/nilRepresentation":{"abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nilRepresentation"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/nilRepresentation","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"nilRepresentation","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/clformat/clformatconfig/nilrepresentation"},"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/setArgumentFactory(makeArguments:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Determines what ","type":"text"},{"code":"makeArguments","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is eventually invoking.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"setArgumentFactory"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"makeArguments"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation6LocaleV","text":"Locale"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":", ["},{"kind":"keyword","text":"Any"},{"kind":"text","text":"?], "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8CLFormat9ArgumentsC","text":"Arguments"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/setArgumentFactory(makeArguments:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"setArgumentFactory(makeArguments:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/clformat/clformatconfig/setargumentfactory(makearguments:)"},"doc://CLFormat/documentation/CLFormat/CLFormatConfig/standard":{"abstract":[{"text":"The standard format configuration. Whenever ","type":"text"},{"cod